  "text": "\r\n\t\t Polling Locations & Ward Information  | Nashua, NH \r\n Skip to Main Content \r\nCreate a Website Account   - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.    \r\nWebsite Sign In \r\n\t\t\t Search \n     Services   \t\t\t \n     Community   \t\t\t \n     Government   \t\t\t \n     I Want To...   \t\t\t \r\nHome \nGovernment \nCity Departments A-M \nCity Clerk's Office \nElections & Voter Registration \nWhere Do I Vote? \r\nPolling Locations & Ward Information \t\t \r\nWhere Do I Vote? \nIn accordance with federal and state law, and the city charter, the Board of Aldermen revised its ward boundaries on December 28, 2021, following the 10-year census so that the populations in each of the wards is \"as equal as circumstances will admit\" (NH Constitution, part Second, Article 9). \nOur polling locations are open from 6:00 AM - 8:00 PM on Election Day.  \nSearch - by street address or street name - to find your ward and voting location. \nVisit the  Board of Aldermen webpage  to see who represents your ward. \nThe following list includes the polling locations for each of the 9 total wards: \nMaster Street List (PDF) \nWard 1 :  \nNashua High School North, 8 Titan Way \nWard 1 Street List (PDF) \nWard 2 :  \nCharlotte Avenue Elementary School, 48 Charlotte Avenue \nWard 2 Street List (PDF) \nWard 3 :  \nAmherst Street Elementary School, 71 Amherst Street \nWard 3 Street List (PDF) \nWard 4 :  \nLedge Street Elementary School, 139 Ledge Street \nWard 4 Street List (PDF) \nWard 5 :  \nNashua High School South, 36 Riverside Street \nWard 5 Street List (PDF) \nWard 6 :  \nFairgrounds Middle School, 27 Cleveland Street \nWard 6 Street List (PDF) \nWard 7 :  \nDr. Norman Crisp Elementary School, 50 Arlington Street \nWard 7 Street List (PDF) \nWard 8 :  \nBicentennial Elementary School, 296 East Dunstable Road \nWard 8 Street List (PDF) \nWard 9 :  \nNew Searles Elementary School, 39 Shady Lane \nWard 9 Street List (PDF) \nCitywide Ward Maps \nNashua Ward Map (PDF)  of polling locations is available for viewing. \r\n\t\t\t Legal Notices \r\n\t\t\t Where Do I Vote? \r\n\t\t\t Election Results \r\n\t\t\t Campaign Information \r\n\t\t\t\t Municipal Campaign Receipt & Expenditure Reports \r\n\t\t\t\t Incumbent Filings \r\n\t\t\t Pay Bills \r\n\t\t\t Alerts & \nNotifications \r\n\t\t\t Motor Vehicle \r\n\t\t\t Road Work \nNews \r\n\t\t\t Maps / GIS \r\n\t\t\t Agendas \n& Minutes \nPortal \r\n\t\t\t Assessing \nValues & Taxes \r\n\t\t\t City Clerk  \nVital Records \r\n\t\t\t Trash & \nRecycling \r\n\t\t\t Budget & \nFinancial \nReports \r\n\t\t\t Public Record & Service Requests \r\n\t\t\t Bus Routes \n& Schedules \r\nContact Us \r\n229 Main Street \nNashua, NH 03060 \nCity Government   \n  Directions to City Hall   \n  Emergency Alert System \r\nQuick Links \r\n         City Officials \n         Elections \n         Career Opportunities \n         ADA Services \n         Ordinances & Resolutions \n/QuickLinks.aspx \r\nHelpful Links \r\n         Home \n         Site Map \n         Contact Us \n         Accessibility \n         Employee Email Access \n         Employee Self Service \n         Privacy Policy \n/QuickLinks.aspx \r\n   Government Websites by  CivicPlus® \nLoading \r\n\t\t\t\tLoading\r\n\t\t\t Do Not Show Again \r\n\t\t\t Close \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Left \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Right \r\n[] \r\n                     Slideshow Left Arrow \r\n                     Slideshow Right Arrow \r\n ",
